As spotted <a href="https://x.com/hiddecollee7/status/2113011414126194966">by Hidde Collee</a>, the <a href="https://www.apple.com/apple-music/">Apple Music page</a> on Apple's website now has the updated branding that Apple <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/10/21/apple-music-new-look-announced/">officially introduced earlier today</a>.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/10/Apple-Music-New-Logo-on-Website.jpg" alt="" width="1600" height="900" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1072051" /><br/>
Apple Music has a new black-and-white logo and app icon, with Apple doing away with the red color scheme that it previously used for the streaming music service.<br/>
<br/>
In a <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=1XxNXkOHKZw">YouTube video</a> released earlier today, Apple showed how the new Apple Music visuals were "made by sound." The video showed off the new Apple Music logo with colorful animations, despite the <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/10/13/ios-27-2-apple-music-icon/">new Apple Music app icon in the iOS 27.2 beta</a> having a more basic black-and-white design. It is unclear if a splash of color will be added later.<br/>
<br/>
<div class="center-wrap"><img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/10/apple-music-icon-1.jpg" alt="" width="1600" height="900" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1070915" /><em>Apple Music's new app icon on the iOS 27.2 beta on the left, old icon on the right</em></div><br/>
Apple Music has also received a distinct font with a modern, impactful aesthetic.<br/>
<br/>
